      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I understand the test. It verifies that `DayOfYear.of(366)` (the last day, only valid in leap years) reports `isValidYear(-488)` as `true` because -488 is a leap year. I'll improve readability with meaningful variable names, assertion messages, and a clarifying comment.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored test uses descriptive variable names (`leapYearLastDay`, `isValidInLeapYear`), adds a clarifying comment explaining why year -488 qualifies as a leap year, and includes assertion messages that make test failures easier to diagnose — all without changing the runtime behavior."
